text:
{"verdict":"The happy path mostly works: both answers get route, dates, ROC-year conversion and kind right. But the output can mislead riders in ways the UI will draw as fact. A non-route like 所有路線 becomes a route chip, the stop to skip and the stop to use instead land in one undifferentiated list, and `short` largely re-reads the notice and repeats the chips instead of telling the rider what to do.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"A phrase meaning 'every route' is returned as a route name. clean() keeps it because the text contains it, so the UI draws a route chip called 所有路線, and any route-matching logic code runs on it fails.","evidence":"Example 1: "routes":["所有路線"] from 本公司所有路線今日（11/10）下午4時起停駛","fix":"Tell the model to return routes [] with scope "全部" when the notice covers every route. Add a scope field to the schema. Have clean() reject 所有/全部/全線 as route names."},{"severity":"high","what":"Stops riders lose and the stop they should use instead are mixed in one list. A UI showing 'affected stops' would send riders to the replacement stop as if it were closed, or to a closed stop as if it were open.","evidence":"Example 0: "stops":["臺北車站(忠孝)站","北門站","臺北車站(青島)站"]. The first two are 暫停停靠; the third is 請改至…搭乘.","fix":"Split into stops (skipped, moved or closed) and instead (where to go). Add instead to the schema. In clean(), drop any stop that also appears in instead."},{"severity":"medium","what":"`short` restates the notice and the chips (routes, times, the 另行公告 boilerplate) instead of the rider's action. It also mangles names and wording.","evidence":"Example 1 short "今日下午4時起全線停駛，恢復時間另行公告。" is the notice body nearly verbatim, and the time is already in from. Example 0 short repeats 307 and the stop list, says "暫停停靠" (doubled 停), and shortens names to "忠孝站"/"青島站", which are not the stops' real names.","fix":"Define `short` as what the rider must do differently: which way to go, where to board. Tell it not to repeat route names, dates or times, and to name a stop only as written and only when it is where to go. Require 台灣用語 and 全形標點 and ban notice boilerplate."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Date rules are implicit, so a cheap model is left guessing. The prompt never covers 民國 years, dates without a year, 今日/明日, or times like 首班車. It also demands HH:MM even when no clock time is given, which pushes the model to invent 00:00, although clean() already accepts a date alone.","evidence":"Prompt: "from / to: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM when it starts and ends". Example 0 needed 115年→2026 and 22時→22:00, and Example 1 needed 今日（11/10）→2026-11-10, with no instruction for either.","fix":"Spell it out: add 1911 to ROC years; take the year from Today for 11/10, 今日 or 明日; use 24-hour HH:MM only when a clock time is stated, otherwise YYYY-MM-DD alone; return "" for 另行公告."},{"severity":"medium","what":"`kind` is not checked against the allowed list in clean(), so any 8-character string reaches the UI. The prompt also leaves cause versus effect open: road works that reroute a bus could be tagged 施工 instead of 改道.","evidence":"clean: kind: str(raw?.kind, 8). Prompt: "kind: one of 停駛 改道 施工 …" with no rule. Example 0's notice has both 施工 (cause) and 改經 (effect).","fix":"Have clean() keep kind only if it is in the list, else use 其他. In the prompt, say kind is what riders experience, not the cause, and that 施工 is only for works that are the change itself, such as an exit closing."},{"severity":"low","what":"The direction restriction is lost. Only 往撫遠街方向 is affected, but a bare 307 chip implies the whole route changes.","evidence":"Example 0 body: 307往撫遠街方向改經中山北路行駛; routes: ["307"]","fix":"Require `short` to name the direction when only one direction changes."},{"severity":"low","what":"clean() allows `short` up to 60 characters while the prompt asks for ≤30 字, so overlong lines pass into a UI built for one line.","evidence":"short: str(raw?.short, 60) vs prompt "one line ≤ 30 字"","fix":"Cap at 40 in clean(), leaving slack for full-width punctuation."}],"edits":[{"old":"'routes: the route or line names it affects, exactly as written (e.g. 307, 紅2, 板南線); stops: stop or station names it names; from / to: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM when it starts and ends ("" when not said); kind: one of 停駛 改道 施工 停靠調整 班次調整 票價 其他; short: one line ≤ 30 字 of what a rider must know.',","new":"'routes: names of the routes or lines the change applies to, copied exactly as written (e.g. 307, 紅2, 板南線). Never a phrase like 所有路線, 全部路線 or 全線. If it applies to every route, routes is [] and scope is "全部"; otherwise scope is "指定".',
          'stops: stops or stations riders lose or that change (skipped, moved, closed), copied exactly as written including brackets (e.g. 臺北車站(忠孝)站). instead: stops the notice tells riders to use instead, copied exactly. Never put a stop in both lists.',
          'from / to: when the change starts and ends. Convert 民國 years by adding 1911 (115年 → 2026). For a date with no year (11/10) or 今日/明日, use Today. Write YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM (24-hour) only if a clock time is stated (22時 → 22:00, 下午4時 → 16:00); otherwise YYYY-MM-DD only, never an invented 00:00. Use "" when not said or 另行公告.',
          'kind: exactly one of 停駛 改道 施工 停靠調整 班次調整 票價 其他, describing what riders experience, not the cause. Road works that reroute a bus are 改道. Use 施工 only when the works themselves are the change (e.g. an exit or elevator closed).',
          'short: one line ≤ 30 字, 台灣用語 and 全形標點, saying what the rider must do differently: which way the bus goes now, where to board instead, which direction is affected. Do not repeat route names, dates or times, or list the skipped stops; those are shown separately. Name a stop only where to go instead, exactly as written. No 敬請見諒, 請注意 or 另行公告.',","why":"Gives the cheap model explicit rules for all-routes notices, skipped versus replacement stops, ROC and relative dates, cause versus effect, and a short line that adds the rider's action rather than repeating chips."},{"old":"schema: obj({ routes: arr(S), stops: arr(S), from: S, to: S, kind: S, short: S }),","new":"schema: obj({ routes: arr(S), scope: S, stops: arr(S), instead: arr(S), from: S, to: S, kind: S, short: S }),","why":"Adds a place to say 'all routes' and a separate list of replacement stops."},{"old":"const routes = list(raw?.routes, 40).map(r => str(r, 20)).filter(r => r && all.includes(r));","new":"const routes = list(raw?.routes, 40).map(r => str(r, 20)).filter(r => r && all.includes(r) && !/所有|全部|全線/.test(r));","why":"Stops 所有路線-style phrases from being drawn as route chips."},{"old":"const stops = list(raw?.stops, 40).map(r => str(r, 30)).filter(r => r && all.includes(r));","new":"const instead = list(raw?.instead, 10).map(r => str(r, 30)).filter(r => r && all.includes(r));
      const stops = list(raw?.stops, 40).map(r => str(r, 30)).filter(r => r && all.includes(r) && !instead.includes(r));","why":"Keeps replacement stops separate and never shows a stop as both closed and the place to go."},{"old":"return { routes, stops, from: when(raw?.from), to: when(raw?.to), kind: str(raw?.kind, 8), short: str(raw?.short, 60) };","new":"const kinds = ['停駛', '改道', '施工', '停靠調整', '班次調整', '票價', '其他'];
      const kind = kinds.includes(raw?.kind) ? raw.kind : '其他';
      return { routes, scope: raw?.scope === '全部' ? '全部' : '指定', stops, instead, from: when(raw?.from), to: when(raw?.to), kind, short: str(raw?.short, 40) };","why":"Checks kind against the allowed set, passes scope and instead through, and caps short closer to the 30-字 limit."}],"examples":[{"name":"All routes, typhoon","input":"{"title":"颱風停駛公告","body":"因颱風影響，本公司所有路線明日（11/11）首班車起停駛，恢復時間另行公告。","today":"2026-11-10"}","expect":"routes [], scope "全部", kind 停駛, from "2026-11-11" with no invented time, to "". short is an action such as 明天全線停駛，請改搭其他交通工具; it must not repeat 另行公告 or the date."},{"name":"ROC date, no clock time, stop moved","input":"{"title":"紅2路公車站位調整","body":"自115年12月1日起，紅2「捷運劍潭站」站位由中山北路側遷移至基河路側，請旅客留意。","today":"2026-11-20"}","expect":"routes ["紅2"], stops ["捷運劍潭站"], instead [], kind 停靠調整, from "2026-12-01" with no 00:00, to "". short says to board on the 基河路 side and must not restate the date."},{"name":"Year rollover from Today","input":"{"title":"235路線跨年夜改道","body":"12/31 20時至1/1 2時，因跨年活動交通管制，235往新店方向改經基隆路行駛，暫停靠市府站，請至臨時站位「松仁路口」候車。","today":"2026-12-28"}","expect":"from "2026-12-31 20:00", to "2027-01-01 02:00", kind 改道 (not 施工 or 其他), stops ["市府站"], instead ["松仁路口"]. short mentions that only the 往新店 direction changes and where to wait."},{"name":"MRT works that are the change itself","input":"{"title":"江子翠站2號出口施工封閉","body":"板南線江子翠站2號出口因電扶梯更新工程，自115年11月16日至116年1月15日封閉，請改由1號或3號出口進出。","today":"2026-11-10"}","expect":"routes ["板南線"], stops ["江子翠站"], kind 施工, from "2026-11-16", to "2027-01-15". short says to use exit 1 or 3 and must not invent times or exit numbers not in the text."},{"name":"Fare change, no stops","input":"{"title":"幹線公車票價調整","body":"敦化幹線、信義幹線自116年1月1日起全票由15元調整為20元，學生票及敬老票不變。","today":"2026-11-10"}","expect":"routes ["敦化幹線","信義幹線"], stops [], kind 票價, from "2027-01-01". short gives the new full fare and that discount tickets are unchanged, using only the figures 15 and 20 from the text; no other numbers."},{"name":"Notice with no rider change","input":"{"title":"悠遊卡乘車滿額抽獎活動","body":"即日起至11月30日，搭乘本公司路線使用悠遊卡累積滿10次即可參加抽獎。","today":"2026-11-10"}","expect":"routes [], scope "指定", stops [], kind 其他; any dates must come from the text. It must not label the notice as a service change, and short must not invent prizes or amounts."}]}

{"verdict":"Not ready to ship. The prompt tells the model to skip 'the lines before the note in brackets', but the facts contain no such note, so it cannot tell what the card already shows. As a result the model ran past the length limit with two tips in Example 0, ignored an overspent month in Example 1, and clean() lets the over-long answer through.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"The prompt points to a bracketed note that the digest never contains, so the model cannot tell card lines from new lines. It also lists patterns (weekends, small buys, biggest buy) that may not exist in the facts, which invites the model to invent them.","evidence":"Prompt: "The person already sees the lines before the note in brackets … Build it on what only the lines after the note show (weekends against weekdays, the small buys, the biggest one…)". Neither example's facts has any [ ] note, nor any weekend, small-buy or biggest-buy line.","fix":"Name the card lines by their labels (Spent / Income / Most went to). Tell the model to build only on the other lines that are actually present, and never to mention a pattern no line states."},{"severity":"high","what":"Ignores the length limit and the 'ONE suggestion' rule, and clean() lets the result through.","evidence":"Example 0's tip is about 53 字, against a limit of ≤ 45. It holds two separate tips: "少去路易莎一次…；購物也先列清單再買，逛街時…先放購物車隔一天". clean() only caps at str(raw?.tip, 160).","fix":"Ask for one action in one sentence. In clean(), reject (rather than truncate) any tip over 60 chars in zh or 180 in en."},{"severity":"high","what":"Misses the one thing that matters most: spending exceeded income. The tip also doesn't use the visible frequency signal.","evidence":"Example 1 facts: "Income 2000; spent more than that" and "7-ELEVEN: 14 times". The tip is a generic "每週挑一天自己備餐…看看餐飲會不會少些" and never speaks to the gap.","fix":"When spending passed income, the action should aim at closing that gap through the place or category that grew most or was visited most. Keep it kind; no lecture."},{"severity":"medium","what":"The tips are generic, not built on the specific signal in the facts.","evidence":"Example 0: "購物也先列清單再買" is stock advice that would fit any month. Example 1's line "7-ELEVEN的消費改成事先備好的飲料" is clumsy and vague.","fix":"Require one small action tied to a named place or category from the non-card lines, phrased as something to try."},{"severity":"medium","what":"The number guard can be bypassed with Chinese numerals, and invented digit targets get rejected, wasting a paid call.","evidence":"numbersFrom only checks digits. A tip like "少花一千" would pass the check, while "每次少花 50" fails and returns null. The prompt only says "Any number you write must appear in the figures".","fix":"Ask for no numbers by preference. Forbid invented amounts or targets in digits or in Chinese numerals, and give an example of each."},{"severity":"low","what":"Full-width punctuation is not requested.","evidence":"The prompt says only "Traditional Chinese (台灣用語)"; the family rule requires 全形標點.","fix":"Add 全形標點 to the language instruction."}],"edits":[{"old":"`Write ONE suggestion for next month in ${en ? 'English, ≤ 25 words' : 'Traditional Chinese (台灣用語), ≤ 45 字'}: honest, kind and concrete. The person already sees the lines before the note in brackets on the same card: never restate them. Build it on what only the lines after the note show (weekends against weekdays, the small buys, the biggest one, the place, what grew inside a category), saying what to try, not the figure again. Not a lecture; no investing or borrowing advice; no markdown.`","new":"`Write ONE suggestion for next month in ${en ? 'English, one sentence, at most 25 words' : 'Traditional Chinese (台灣用語，全形標點), one sentence, at most 45 字'}: honest, kind and concrete. Give exactly one small action to try, tied to a place or category named in the facts. The card already shows the lines starting "Spent", "Income" and "Most went to" (and any line before a [bracketed] note): never repeat those figures or say the month went up or down. Base the action on the other lines only (what grew most, the place visited most, and any other line given). Never mention weekends, small buys, a biggest buy or any pattern unless a line states it. If the Income line says spending passed income, aim the action at closing that gap through the place or category that grew most or was visited most, without scolding. Not a lecture; no investing, borrowing or credit advice; no markdown.`","why":"The bracket note never appears in the facts, so the model now gets the card lines by label. It is told to use only lines that exist, the overspent case gets priority, and one sentence plus full-width punctuation are required."},{"old":"'Any number you write must appear in the figures exactly (no thousands commas, no new sums or percentages).'","new":"'Prefer no numbers at all. If you write one, copy it exactly from the facts (no thousands commas). Never invent an amount, target, sum or percentage, in digits or in Chinese numerals (not "少花 200", not "少花一千"); a count of actions in words such as 少去一次 is fine.'","why":"Closes the Chinese-numeral bypass and stops the model inventing targets that numbersFrom would reject, wasting a call."},{"old":"clean: (raw, { facts }) => {
      const tip = str(raw?.tip, 160);
      return tip && numbersFrom(tip, facts) ? { tip } : null;","new":"clean: (raw, { facts, en }) => {
      const tip = str(raw?.tip, 400);
      if (!tip || tip.length > (en ? 180 : 60)) return null;
      return numbersFrom(tip, facts) ? { tip } : null;","why":"The 160-char cap let a 53-字 two-tip answer through for a 45-字 card line. Reject over-long answers instead of showing or truncating them."}],"examples":[{"name":"overspent, frequent convenience store","input":"{"facts":"Month: 2026-11. Amounts are NT$.\nSpent 5120; the month before 4300\nIncome 3000; spent more than that\nMost went to 餐飲: 3010\nUp most on the month before: 餐飲 2400 → 3010 (more 610)\nWent most often to 全家: 18 times, 1460"}","expect":"One sentence of 45 字 or fewer, with full-width punctuation, giving one action around 全家 visits or 餐飲 that would help close the gap with income. Must not restate 5120, 3000 or 3010, invent a target like 少花 500, or scold."},{"name":"English phone","input":"{"facts":"Month: 2026-11. Amounts are NT$.\nSpent 8800; the month before 7900\nIncome 12000; kept 27% of it\nMost went to 交通: 3200\nUp most on the month before: 娛樂 900 → 1850 (more 950)\nWent most often to Uber: 9 times, 1620","lang":"en"}","expect":"One English sentence of 25 words or fewer, with an action on Uber rides or the jump in 娛樂. Must not repeat 8800, 12000, 27% or 3200, and no investing advice."},{"name":"weekend and small-buy lines present","input":"{"facts":"Month: 2026-11. Amounts are NT$.\nSpent 15400; the month before 14800\nIncome 30000; kept 49% of it\nMost went to 餐飲: 6200\nWeekends 7900 over 8 days; weekdays 7500 over 22 days\nSmall buys under 100: 41 times, 2380\nBiggest one: 耳機 2490 at 燦坤"}","expect":"Builds on the weekend-heavy spending or the 41 small buys, as one action. Any number used is copied exactly, e.g. 41. No new per-day averages or percentages, and does not mention 15400 or 6200."},{"name":"only card lines, nothing extra","input":"{"facts":"Month: 2026-11. Amounts are NT$.\nSpent 6100; the month before 6050\nIncome 9000; kept 32% of it\nMost went to 餐飲: 2900"}","expect":"No restated figures. Must not invent weekend, small-buy or store patterns. At most a light action on 餐飲 with no numbers, otherwise an empty tip so clean() drops it."},{"name":"good month, spending down","input":"{"facts":"Month: 2026-11. Amounts are NT$.\nSpent 9200; the month before 13400\nIncome 25000; kept 63% of it\nMost went to 餐飲: 4100\nUp most on the month before: 日用品 600 → 1100 (more 500)\nWent most often to 85度C: 7 times, 455"}","expect":"Kind and not alarmist. One concrete idea, e.g. on 日用品 growth or 85度C visits; 85 is fine because it is part of the store name. Must not invent 每次少花 30 or restate 9200, 13400 or 63%."},{"name":"facts with bracketed card note","input":"{"facts":"Month: 2026-11. Amounts are NT$.\nSpent 21000; the month before 18000\nIncome 40000; kept 47% of it\nMost went to 購物: 7800\n[shown above on the card]\nUp most on the month before: 購物 4200 → 7800 (more 3600)\nWent most often to 蝦皮: 11 times, 5300"}","expect":"Treats every line before the note as already seen. One action about 蝦皮 orders or the 購物 rise, e.g. 下單前先放購物車一天, as a single tip of 45 字 or fewer. Must not stack two tips."}]}

{"verdict":"Only one of three answers is right. Example 1 is clean, but Example 0 invents a comeback by misreading the run's starting score, and Example 2 calls a run that began with the Warriors up 29 the turn that decided the game. The prompt never explains how to read the facts and gives the model a list of story types with no rule for which one actually decided the game.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"The model misreads the run's starting score and invents a comeback. In "(from 29-24 for them)" the running team's points come first, so the Rockets were already ahead 29-24. The answer says they were behind.","evidence":"Facts: "Biggest run: {t:10} 14-0, Q1 2.6 to Q2 8:08 (from 29-24 for them)". Answer: "{t:10}以14-0攻勢自29-24落後反超" / "{t:10} erased a 29-24 deficit with a 14-0 run". Example 1 confirms the format: the Pacers' run "from 45-48 for them" ends at Mavericks 50-63. numbersFrom() passes the answer because 29-24 is in the facts.","fix":"Spell out each fact format in the prompt: the score is from before the run, the running team's score comes first, and only "came back from N down" means the winner trailed. Also ban 反超, 逆轉 and 'erased a deficit' unless the winner was behind or level just before."},{"severity":"high","what":"The model picks a run that started deep in a blowout as the turn that decided the game. The prompt lists story types but never says which one to choose, or when a run doesn't count.","evidence":"Example 2 facts: "{t:9} ahead for good: Q1 10:49, 5-3" and "Biggest run ... (from 90-61 for them)", plus "won the Q3 40-22". Answer: "第三節 {t:9} 打出 13-0 攻勢改寫比賽" / "broke it open with a 13-0 run". The Warriors were already up 29 and led from the first quarter on. Nothing was 改寫.","fix":"Give an explicit order: comeback, then a late lead for good, then a run that changed the lead or opened the gap that held, then (for teams that led from Q1 or Q2) 'led from then on' plus the period they won big. State that a run starting 15 or more points up, or a run by the loser, never decided the game."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Example 0 packs two ideas into one line, joined by ；, and is likely over the 40-字 limit. clean() never checks length, so an over-long line would still be drawn on the card.","evidence":""…{p:4433192}獨得其中7分；第三節4:14靠其兩分球以62-60超前後未再易主。" is about 50 字 without tokens. The prompt asks for "One idea, not a list" and "≤ 40 字".","fix":"Require a single sentence and forbid joining facts with ；. In clean(), reject zh over 48 characters without tokens and en over 26 words."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Clock times come out without 剩 (time left), which is unclear and not how a Taiwan sports desk writes them. The prompt never says that facts times are time left in the period, or that "2.6" means seconds.","evidence":""第四節9:36由{p:6442}三分反超" and "第三節4:14靠其兩分球". Facts: "Q1 2.6 to Q2 8:08".","fix":"Explain that clock times are time left and show the format 「第三節剩4:14」 in zh and "with 4:14 left in the third" in en. Keep the digits exactly as the facts give them, so the number check still passes."},{"severity":"low","what":"The zh lines break the 全形標點 and Taiwan typesetting rule: they add half-width spaces around tokens and numbers and leave off the closing 。.","evidence":"Example 2: "第三節 {t:9} 打出 13-0 攻勢改寫比賽，{p:3975} 包辦其中 7 分". Example 1 also has no closing 「。」.","fix":"In the prompt, say no spaces around tokens or numbers and end with 「。」."},{"severity":"low","what":"Nothing stops the model from typing a team's name in English, citing win-chance points, or naming a player who has no token. Every player in these examples happens to have a token, so none of this has been tested.","evidence":"clean() checks only last names taken from "{p:..} = Name". Team names such as "(Houston Rockets)" are never checked. Win-chance figures like "+18 pts" are in the facts, so numbersFrom() would accept them.","fix":"In the prompt, forbid writing win-chance points and naming any player without a {p:} token. In clean(), also reject en that contains a word from a team's name."}],"edits":[{"old":"From the facts below, say the turn that decided it, as a sports desk in Taiwan would: a run and who drove it, a comeback from how far down, when the winner went ahead for good and on whose play, the period that broke it open, a late swing. One idea, not a list.","new":"How to read the facts: "ahead for good" names the winner. Clock times are time LEFT in the period (Q3 4:14 = 4:14 left in the 3rd; a bare 2.6 = 2.6 seconds left). In a run, "(from 29-24 for them)" is the score just BEFORE the run with the running team's points FIRST: 29-24 means they were already AHEAD by 5, not behind. Only "came back from N down" says the winner trailed. "home win chance ±N pts" is only to judge how big a play was; never write it.
Pick ONE turn, the first that fits: (1) a comeback: how far down, and the run or play that got them ahead for good; (2) a lead for good taken in Q4 or OT: when and on whose play; (3) a run by the winner that took them from behind or level to ahead, or opened the gap that held; (4) if the winner was ahead for good from Q1 or Q2: that they led from then on, plus the period they won big. A run that began with the team already up 15 or more, or a run by the loser, did not decide the game; never call it the turn.
Say it as a sports desk in Taiwan would: one idea in one sentence, never a list of facts joined by ；.","why":"Fixes the run-score misread in Example 0 and the blowout run in Example 2 by explaining the fact formats and giving a fixed order for choosing the turn."},{"old":"zh: ONE line in Traditional Chinese (台灣的體育報導用語), ≤ 40 字 not counting tokens, no English words. en: the same line in English, ≤ 22 words.","new":"zh: ONE sentence in Traditional Chinese as a Taiwan sports desk writes it (台灣體育報導用語、全形標點，句末加「。」), ≤ 40 字 not counting tokens, no English words, no spaces around tokens or numbers. Write clock times as 「第三節剩4:14」 and scores as 「62-60」, digits exactly as the facts give them. en: the same sentence in English, ≤ 22 words, times as "with 4:14 left in the third".","why":"Makes clock times say 剩 (time left) and makes zh follow Taiwan typesetting: full-width punctuation, a closing 。, and no spaces around tokens or numbers."},{"old":"Use only these facts. Every number you write must be one of theirs. No adjectives the facts don’t support.","new":"Use only these facts. Every number you write must be one of theirs. No adjectives the facts don’t support: 反超, 逆轉, 改寫, 'erased a deficit' or 'broke it open' only when the facts show it. Name only players who have a {p:} token under Players; anyone else stays unnamed. Never write win-chance points.","why":"Blocks the invented 落後反超 and 改寫比賽 claims, the untokened player names and the win-chance figures, none of which the number check can catch."},{"old":"      if (names.some(n => bare(en).includes(n))) return null;","new":"      if (names.some(n => bare(en).includes(n))) return null;
      const teamWords = [...facts.matchAll(/\{t:[^}]+\} = \w+ \(([^)]+)\)/g)].flatMap(m => m[1].split(/\s+/)).filter(n => n.length >= 4);
      if (teamWords.some(n => bare(en).includes(n))) return null;
      if (bare(zh).replace(/\s/g, '').length > 48 || en.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length > 26) return null;","why":"Rejects team names typed out in the English line and lines too long for the card, which the old clean() let through."}],"examples":[{"name":"winner's run while already ahead","input":"{"facts":"NBA (basketball)\nTeams: {t:2} = home (Boston Celtics); {t:18} = away (New York Knicks)\nLead changes: 4; ties: 3\n{t:2} ahead for good: Q2 6:40, 41-39, on {p:4065648}'s play (Jayson Tatum makes 18-foot pullup jump shot (Derrick White assists))\nBiggest run: {t:2} 12-0, Q2 3:02 to Q2 0:31 (from 50-47 for them), {p:3078576} 6 of them\n{t:2} won the Q3 31-20\nPlays that swung the win chance most:\n2nd Quarter 6:40 Jayson Tatum makes 18-foot pullup jump shot (Derrick White assists) (home win chance +6 pts)\n1st Quarter 4:12 Jalen Brunson makes 3-foot driving layup (home win chance -4 pts)\nPlayers: {p:4065648} = Jayson Tatum; {p:3078576} = Derrick White; {p:3934672} = Jalen Brunson"}","expect":"Must not say {t:2} was behind or 反超 during the 12-0 run; they were already up 50-47. It may say the run opened the gap that held, or that they led for good from 第二節剩6:40 on {p:4065648}'s shot. One idea only, no win-chance points, no spaces around tokens, and zh ends with 。."},{"name":"overtime decider, untokened player","input":"{"facts":"NBA (basketball)\nTeams: {t:25} = home (Oklahoma City Thunder); {t:13} = away (Los Angeles Lakers)\nLead changes: 14; ties: 9\n{t:25} ahead for good: OT 0:48, 118-117, on {p:4278073}'s play (Shai Gilgeous-Alexander makes 14-foot step back jumpshot)\nBiggest run: {t:13} 10-0, Q4 4:20 to Q4 1:55 (from 98-103 for them)\nPlays that swung the win chance most:\nOT 0:48 Shai Gilgeous-Alexander makes 14-foot step back jumpshot (home win chance +31 pts)\nOT 0:05 Luguentz Dort blocks LeBron James's 6-foot layup (home win chance +22 pts)\nPlayers: {p:4278073} = Shai Gilgeous-Alexander; {p:1966} = LeBron James"}","expect":"Must tell the overtime go-ahead: 延長賽剩0:48, 118-117, on {p:4278073}'s shot. It may mention the block late in overtime, but must not name Dort, who has no token, in words or transliteration. No 'Thunder' or 'Lakers' in en, no 31 or 22 win-chance figures. The Lakers' run is not the turn."},{"name":"wire-to-wire blowout, garbage-time run","input":"{"facts":"NBA (basketball)\nTeams: {t:5} = home (Cleveland Cavaliers); {t:30} = away (Washington Wizards)\nLead changes: 0; ties: 0\n{t:5} ahead for good: Q1 11:21, 2-0, on {p:3908809}'s play (Donovan Mitchell makes driving layup)\nBiggest run: {t:5} 15-0, Q4 6:00 to Q4 2:10 (from 112-80 for them), {p:4432174} 8 of them\n{t:5} won the Q2 38-19\nPlays that swung the win chance most:\n1st Quarter 11:21 Donovan Mitchell makes driving layup (home win chance +3 pts)\nPlayers: {p:3908809} = Donovan Mitchell; {p:4432174} = Craig Porter Jr."}","expect":"The story is that {t:5} led from the opening minute and the second quarter, 38-19, broke it open. It must not present the Q4 15-0 run, which began 112-80, as the turn. Every number must come from the facts."},{"name":"real comeback driven by a run","input":"{"facts":"NBA (basketball)\nTeams: {t:21} = home (Phoenix Suns); {t:24} = away (San Antonio Spurs)\nLead changes: 3; ties: 2\n{t:21} came back from 18 down (52-70, Q3 7:12)\n{t:21} ahead for good: Q4 2:05, 101-99, on {p:3136193}'s play (Devin Booker makes 22-foot jumper)\nBiggest run: {t:21} 16-0, Q3 6:50 to Q3 1:15 (from 52-70 for them), {p:3136193} 9 of them\n{t:21} trailed by 4 going into the Q4\nPlays that swung the win chance most:\n4th Quarter 2:05 Devin Booker makes 22-foot jumper (home win chance +15 pts)\nPlayers: {p:3136193} = Devin Booker; {p:5104157} = Victor Wembanyama"}","expect":"Must tell the comeback from 18 down: either the 16-0 run with {p:3136193}'s 9, or the go-ahead with 2:05 left in Q4 at 101-99. One sentence, not both joined by ；. Comeback words are correct here. zh ≤ 40 字."},{"name":"nothing beyond the score","input":"{"facts":"NBA (basketball)\nTeams: {t:8} = home (Detroit Pistons); {t:20} = away (Philadelphia 76ers)\nLead changes: 0; ties: 0\nPlayers: {p:4432166} = Cade Cunningham"}","expect":"Must return zh "" and en "". No made-up run, period or play, and no naming of {p:4432166}."},{"name":"loser's big run, late winner","input":"{"facts":"NBA (basketball)\nTeams: {t:14} = home (Miami Heat); {t:1} = away (Atlanta Hawks)\nLead changes: 9; ties: 7\n{t:1} ahead for good: Q4 0:03, 105-104, on {p:4277905}'s play (Trae Young makes 27-foot three point jumper)\nBiggest run: {t:14} 15-0, Q2 9:10 to Q2 4:30 (from 30-33 for them), {p:6430} 8 of them\n{t:1} trailed by 6 going into the Q4\nPlays that swung the win chance most:\n4th Quarter 0:03 Trae Young makes 27-foot three point jumper (home win chance -58 pts)\n4th Quarter 0:20 Jimmy Butler misses driving layup (home win chance -12 pts)\nPlayers: {p:4277905} = Trae Young; {p:6430} = Jimmy Butler"}","expect":"The turn is {t:1} going ahead for good on {p:4277905}'s three with 3 seconds left (第四節剩0:03), 105-104, possibly coming from 6 down into Q4. The Heat's 15-0 run must not be the story, the 58 win-chance figure must not appear, and there must be no 'Heat' or 'Hawks' in en."}]}

{"verdict":"The core loop works on short chats: corrections are minimal, the right words are credited, and replies steer toward an unused word without saying it. A history bug breaks long chats, though, and the prompt leaves several cases undefined: inflected words that clean() silently drops, two-mistake explanations, finished word lists, students asking what a word means, Chinese input, and distress.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"The history keeps the oldest 8 turns instead of the newest. In any chat longer than 4 exchanges the model corrects an old line. If turn 8 happens to be the AI's, input() returns null and the feature stops answering.","evidence":"`const turns = list(raw?.turns, 8)` truncates first. The later `turns.slice(-8)` acts on an array that already has at most 8 items, and `turns.at(-1).who !== 'me'` then tests turn 8, not the student's real last line.","fix":"Slice the raw array from the end before list(): `list(Array.isArray(raw?.turns) ? raw.turns.slice(-8) : [], 8)`."},{"severity":"medium","what":"`used` must echo the list's exact spelling, but the prompt says "any form". When a student writes "deserved" or "abandoned", the model may return that form. clean() matches exact lowercase keys, so the word is dropped and the student never gets credit.","evidence":"Prompt: "used: which of their words their last line uses correctly (in a right meaning, any form)." clean(): `known.get(String(w).toLowerCase().trim())`.","fix":"Tell the model to return each word exactly as written in Their words. Also state that small grammar slips around a correctly meant word still count, as Example 1 already assumes."},{"severity":"medium","what":"`why` explains two mistakes and runs past the 30-字 limit. That is too long for one UI line, and it ignores "main mistake".","evidence":"Example 1: "想表達過去要用 wanted to；because 後面的子句需要動詞 was。" covers two rules.","fix":"Say "the single biggest mistake only, never two" and name the rule without re-quoting the sentence. Add a word limit for the English case too."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Nothing in clean() enforces consistency between fields. If the model returns `why` with an empty `fixed`, or echoes the student's line unchanged as `fixed`, the UI shows a correction chip for a line that was already fine.","evidence":"clean(): `fixed: str(raw?.fixed, 400), why: str(raw?.why, 120)`, with no comparison to the last line and no tie between why and fixed.","fix":"In clean(), set fixed to "" when it equals the student's last line (trimmed, case-insensitive). Set why to "" whenever fixed is empty."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Several cases have no rule. The prompt doesn't say what to do when every word is used. "Never explain them" makes the model stonewall a student who asks what a word means. Nothing covers a line written in Chinese. A student signalling real distress gets cheerful vocabulary steering.","evidence":"Prompt: "one question that gives them a natural chance to use one word not used yet. Never use their words yourself, never explain them, never list them." No other instruction covers these cases.","fix":"Add explicit branches. If all words are used, just chat. If asked about a word, give one everyday example sentence and invite them to try. If the line is mostly Chinese, reply in English and put the English version in fixed. If they show distress, drop the practice and point them kindly to a trusted adult."},{"severity":"low","what":""Not used yet" is ambiguous: it could mean the stored used list or also the words in this turn. A cheap model may target a word the student just used. Yes/no questions also give the student little chance to use the word.","evidence":"Example 1 reply: "Did you get a short break before trying again?" The student can just say "yes" without using brief.","fix":"Require an open question (not yes/no) aimed at a word that is in neither Used well already nor this line."},{"severity":"low","what":"The scope of `fixed` is undefined. A comma splice was kept in Example 2, and a model could equally start correcting casual chat style (lowercase, missing period), which would nag teenagers.","evidence":"Example 2 fixed: "My uncle is very generous, he bought me a new bike."","fix":"List what to fix (grammar, word choice, word form, run-on sentences) and what to ignore (lowercase, a missing final period, contractions)."}],"edits":[{"old":"const turns = list(raw?.turns, 8)","new":"const turns = list(Array.isArray(raw?.turns) ? raw.turns.slice(-8) : [], 8)","why":"Keep the newest 8 turns so the student's real last line is checked and long chats keep working."},{"old":"'fixed: their last line corrected with the fewest changes, "" when it is already natural and correct. Keep their idea.',","new":"'fixed: their last line corrected with the fewest changes, "" when it is already natural and correct. Keep their idea. Fix grammar, word choice, word form and run-on sentences (two sentences joined only by a comma); ignore chat style (lowercase, a missing final period, contractions). If their line is mostly Chinese, put how to say it in natural simple English.',","why":"Defines what counts as a mistake, so the model neither nags about style nor misses run-ons, and covers Chinese input."},{"old":"`why: when fixed, one short line on the main mistake${en ? ', in English' : ', in Traditional Chinese (台灣用語), ≤ 30 字'}; "" otherwise.`,","new":"`why: when fixed, one short line on the single biggest mistake only, never two${en ? ', in English, ≤ 15 words' : ', in Traditional Chinese (台灣用語，全形標點), ≤ 30 字'}; name the rule, do not repeat the fixed sentence; "" when fixed is "".`,","why":"One rule per chip, within the UI length, in both languages."},{"old":"'used: which of their words their last line uses correctly (in a right meaning, any form).',","new":"'used: which of their words their last line uses in a right meaning (any form counts, e.g. abandoned, deserves; small grammar slips around the word are fine). Write each exactly as it appears in Their words, e.g. "abandon" not "abandoned"; [] when none. A word they only ask about, quote or use in a wrong meaning does not count.',","why":"clean() keeps only exact list spellings, and the criteria for credit were vague."},{"old":"'reply: your next line, ≤ 25 words, simple English (CEFR B1): react to what they said, then one question that gives them a natural chance to use one word not used yet. Never use their words yourself, never explain them, never list them.',","new":"'reply: your next line, ≤ 25 words, simple English (CEFR B1): react to what they said in one short sentence, then one open question (not yes/no) that gives them a natural chance to use one word that is neither in Used well already nor in their last line. If every word is used, just keep the chat going with one open question. Never use their words yourself and never list them, except: if they ask what a word means or how to use it, give one short everyday example sentence with it and invite them to try their own. If they write in Chinese, still reply in simple English. If they say something that sounds like real distress (being hurt, wanting to hurt themselves), drop the practice: reply kindly and suggest talking to a parent, teacher or school counselor.',","why":"Covers the target-word ambiguity, a finished word list, questions about meaning, Chinese input and distress."},{"old":"clean: (raw, { words }) => {","new":"clean: (raw, { words, turns }) => {","why":"clean() needs the student's last line to drop no-op corrections."},{"old":"return { fixed: str(raw?.fixed, 400), why: str(raw?.why, 120), used:","new":"const said = String(turns?.at(-1)?.text || '').trim().toLowerCase();
      let fixed = str(raw?.fixed, 400);
      if (fixed.trim().toLowerCase() === said) fixed = '';
      return { fixed, why: fixed ? str(raw?.why, 120) : '', used:","why":"Never show a correction identical to what the student wrote, or an explanation without a correction."}],"examples":[{"name":"long chat keeps the newest line","input":"{"words":["reluctant","abandon","brief","deserve"],"used":["reluctant","brief"],"turns":[{"who":"ai","text":"Hi! How was school today?"},{"who":"me","text":"I was reluctant to go."},{"who":"ai","text":"Oh no, why?"},{"who":"me","text":"We had a test."},{"who":"ai","text":"How did it go?"},{"who":"me","text":"Teacher gave a brief talk first."},{"who":"ai","text":"What did you eat after?"},{"who":"me","text":"Bubble tea with my friends."},{"who":"ai","text":"Nice! Why bubble tea?"},{"who":"me","text":"I think we deserve a treat because we study so hard."}],"lang":"zh"}","expect":"Input is not null. The model sees the 10th turn as the last line: fixed "", why "", used ["deserve"]. The reply targets abandon without saying it. It must not correct an earlier line."},{"name":"inflected form credited in base spelling","input":"{"words":["generous","compete","deserve"],"used":[],"turns":[{"who":"ai","text":"How was your basketball game?"},{"who":"me","text":"We competed with other school and we deserved to win."}],"lang":"zh"}","expect":"used is exactly ["compete","deserve"] (not "competed" or "deserved"). fixed adds "another school" or "other schools". why is one Traditional Chinese line ≤ 30 字 about that single mistake. The reply nudges toward generous without using it."},{"name":"all words used","input":"{"words":["generous","compete"],"used":["generous"],"turns":[{"who":"ai","text":"Do you like sports?"},{"who":"me","text":"Yes, I like to compete in swimming races."}],"lang":"en"}","expect":"fixed "", why "", used ["compete"]. The reply reacts and asks one open question, with no attempt to target a word and no word list. It does not use generous or compete."},{"name":"student asks what a word means, in Chinese","input":"{"words":["reluctant","abandon"],"used":[],"turns":[{"who":"ai","text":"What did you do last weekend?"},{"who":"me","text":"abandon 是什麼意思？"}],"lang":"zh"}","expect":"used is [] (only asked about). fixed gives the English version, like "What does abandon mean?". The reply is in simple English with one short everyday example sentence using abandon, inviting them to try. No dictionary-style definition and no refusal."},{"name":"casual style not nagged, wrong meaning not credited","input":"{"words":["brief","generous"],"used":[],"turns":[{"who":"ai","text":"What's your favorite food?"},{"who":"me","text":"i love beef noodles, the bowl is so generous lol"}],"lang":"zh"}","expect":"No fixes for lowercase or "lol". Generous for a big portion is a valid meaning, so used is ["generous"] and fixed is "" or only a run-on fix. If the line were "my teacher is generous, she is very tall", used would be []. The reply targets brief without saying it."},{"name":"distress signal","input":"{"words":["abandon","deserve"],"used":[],"turns":[{"who":"ai","text":"How are you feeling about school?"},{"who":"me","text":"i feel like i deserve nothing and everyone will abandon me"}],"lang":"zh"}","expect":"The reply is kind, has no word-practice steering, and suggests talking to a parent, teacher or school counselor, in ≤ 25 simple words. fixed is "" or minimal. No cheerful pivot to another topic."}]}

{"verdict":"The common cases come back right: all five answers are correct, and clean() refuses any place the person didn't say or save. Time handling has gaps: a day with no time collapses to 'leave now', a 下週 day becomes today without warning, the model has to work out weekdays itself, and an answer with no place throws away the time the person gave.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"A day with no clock time is lost. 「明天去台中」 must come back as by "now" (the prompt says "now" when no time is said), and clean() then forces day to 0. The trip gets planned for right now, today, which is wrong.","evidence":"Prompt: '"now" when no time is said'. clean(): `const by = ['arrive', 'depart'].includes(raw?.by) && time ? raw.by : 'now';` then `day: by === 'now' ? 0 : day`.","fix":"Let a named day with no time come back as by "depart", time "", day N. clean() keeps it when day > 0, so the phone asks only for the time or shows that day's first departures."},{"severity":"high","what":"A day more than 7 ahead silently becomes today. 「下週六」 said on a Wednesday is 10 days ahead, and clean() turns any day above 7 into 0 instead of refusing it. The prompt never says what 下週X or a same-day weekday means.","evidence":"clean(): `raw.day >= 0 && raw.day <= 7 ? raw.day : 0`. Prompt: 'or the days until a weekday they name' (no 下週, no 'today is that weekday').","fix":"Let code give the model a numbered list of days with 這週/下週 labels, allow 0–14, and return null for anything outside instead of using 0."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Code can compute the weekday, but the model is left to do it. input() only checks that `now` starts with a date. The weekday appears in the examples only because the caller happened to add it, so a 'now' without 週X makes a cheap low-effort model count weekdays from a raw date.","evidence":"input(): `!/^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d \d\d:\d\d/.test(now)` then passes `now` through unchanged. Prompt: 'Now: 2026-11-11 10:00 週三 (Taiwan).' (週三 comes from the caller, not from code).","fix":"In input(), compute the weekday and a table of day numbers (0=今天週三、1=明天週四…5=下週一…) from the date, reject invalid dates, and have the model pick a number from that table."},{"severity":"medium","what":"The prompt has no rule for an hour without 早上/下午/晚上, for 中午/凌晨/半夜十二點, or for a time already past today. 「八點到學校」 at 10:00 would likely come back as 08:00 today, which has already passed.","evidence":"Prompt only lists '早上八點 08:00, 下午三點半 15:30, 晚上 7 點 19:00'.","fix":"Add: with no part-of-day word, take the first such time after Now on that day (at 10:00, 八點 → 20:00). Add the 中午十二點 12:00 and 凌晨/半夜十二點 00:00 (next day) cases."},{"severity":"medium","what":"When no place is said, clean() throws away the day and time the person did say. The phone asks where again, and the time has to be given a second time.","evidence":"Example 4 answer `{"from":"","to":"","by":"depart","day":1,"time":"08:00"}` becomes `{ from: '', to: '', by: 'now', day: 0, time: '' }` in clean().","fix":"Parse time, day and by before the place check and keep them in the empty-place answer. The phone then asks only for the place, offering saved places as taps."},{"severity":"low","what":"The prompt never says that `to` is "" when no place is given. The model guessed it right in Example 4, but a cheap model may instead invent a place or copy 「明天早上八點」 as the destination, and clean() would then throw the whole answer away.","evidence":"Prompt 'to:' line gives no empty case. Example 4: 'They said: 明天早上八點'.","fix":"State: to is "" when they don't say where; never guess one."}],"edits":[{"old":"return { t, now, places: list(raw?.places, 12).map(x => str(x, 30)).filter(Boolean) };","new":"const d0 = new Date(`${now.slice(0, 10)}T12:00:00Z`).getUTCDay();
      if (Number.isNaN(d0)) return null;
      const days = Array.from({ length: 14 }, (_, i) => {
        const wk = Math.floor((((d0 + 6) % 7) + i) / 7);
        return wk < 2 ? `${i}=${['今天', '明天', '後天'][i] || ''}${wk ? '下' : ''}週${'日一二三四五六'[(d0 + i) % 7]}` : '';
      }).filter(Boolean).join('、');
      return { t, now: now.slice(0, 16), days, places: list(raw?.places, 12).map(x => str(x, 30)).filter(Boolean) };","why":"Code computes the weekday and the number for each day through the end of next week, so the model only looks a day up and never counts. Invalid dates are rejected."},{"old":"parts: ({ t, now, places }) =>","new":"parts: ({ t, now, days, places }) =>","why":"The prompt needs the day table that input() now builds."},{"old":"drop words like 到, 去, 前往).","new":"drop words like 到, 去, 前往; "" when they don’t say where, never a guess).","why":"Makes the empty-destination case explicit for cheap models."},{"old":"'by: "arrive" when they must be there by a time (前到, 之前到, 趕上), "depart" when they leave at a time, "now" when no time is said. day: 0 today, 1 tomorrow, 2 the day after, or the days until a weekday they name; time: 24-hour "HH:MM" (早上八點 08:00, 下午三點半 15:30, 晚上 7 點 19:00), "" with by "now".',","new":"'by: "arrive" when they must be there by a time (前到, 之前到, 趕上), "depart" when they leave at a time or only name a day (明天去台中: depart, time ""), "now" when they say no time and no day.',
          'day: the number from the Days list for the day they mean (明天 1, 後天 2; 週六 alone = the next 週六 coming, today if it is that day and the time is still ahead; 下週六 = the one marked 下週六); 0 when no day is said.',
          'time: 24-hour "HH:MM" (早上八點 08:00, 下午三點半 15:30, 晚上 7 點 19:00, 中午十二點 12:00, 凌晨一點 01:00, 半夜十二點 00:00 of the next day). With no 早上/下午/晚上, take the first such time after Now on that day (at 10:00, 八點 today is 20:00). "" when no time is said.',","why":"Covers 下週X, the same weekday as today, hours with no 早上/下午, noon and midnight, and a day with no time. These are the cases the current wording leaves to guessing."},{"old":"`Now: ${now} (Taiwan).`,","new":"`Now: ${now} (Taiwan). Days: ${days}.`,","why":"Gives the model the day table built by code."},{"old":"      const to = str(raw?.to, 40).replace(/^(到|去|前往)/, '');
      // (No place said, said so: an answer, the phone asks again; never a second model.)
      if (!to && raw && typeof raw === 'object' && 'to' in raw) return { from: '', to: '', by: 'now', day: 0, time: '' };
      if (!ok(to)) return null;
      const from0 = str(raw?.from, 40).replace(/^從/, '');
      const from = /^(這裡|這邊|現在位置|目前位置|我的位置)$/.test(from0) || !ok(from0) ? '' : from0;
      const m = /^(\d{1,2}):(\d{2})$/.exec(str(raw?.time, 5));
      const time = m && +m[1] < 24 && +m[2] < 60 ? `${m[1].padStart(2, '0')}:${m[2]}` : '';
      const by = ['arrive', 'depart'].includes(raw?.by) && time ? raw.by : 'now';
      const day = Number.isInteger(raw?.day) && raw.day >= 0 && raw.day <= 7 ? raw.day : 0;
      return { from, to, by, day: by === 'now' ? 0 : day, time: by === 'now' ? '' : time };","new":"      const m = /^(\d{1,2}):(\d{2})$/.exec(str(raw?.time, 5));
      const time = m && +m[1] < 24 && +m[2] < 60 ? `${m[1].padStart(2, '0')}:${m[2]}` : '';
      const day = raw?.day == null ? 0 : Number.isInteger(raw.day) && raw.day >= 0 && raw.day <= 14 ? raw.day : -1;
      if (day < 0) return null;
      const by = ['arrive', 'depart'].includes(raw?.by) && (time || day) ? raw.by : 'now';
      const when = { by, day: by === 'now' ? 0 : day, time: by === 'now' ? '' : time };
      const to = str(raw?.to, 40).replace(/^(到|去|前往)/, '');
      // (No place said: keep the day and time they said; the phone asks only where, saved places as taps; never a second model.)
      if (!to && raw && typeof raw === 'object' && 'to' in raw) return { from: '', to: '', ...when };
      if (!ok(to)) return null;
      const from0 = str(raw?.from, 40).replace(/^從/, '');
      const from = /^(這裡|這邊|現在位置|目前位置|我的位置)$/.test(from0) || !ok(from0) ? '' : from0;
      return { from, to, ...when };","why":"Keeps a named day that has no time (depart, time ""). Allows next-week days (≤14) and refuses an impossible day instead of using today. Keeps the day and time when the place is missing."}],"examples":[{"name":"hour without part of day, already past","input":"{"text":"八點到學校","now":"2026-11-11 10:00","places":["家","學校"]}","expect":"to "學校", by "arrive", time "20:00", day 0. Must not return 08:00 today, which has already passed."},{"name":"day with no time","input":"{"text":"明天去台中","now":"2026-11-11 10:00","places":["家","學校"]}","expect":"to "台中", from "", by "depart", day 1, time "". Must not end up as by "now" with day 0."},{"name":"下週 weekday beyond 7 days","input":"{"text":"下週六早上九點去九份","now":"2026-11-11 10:00","places":[]}","expect":"to "九份", by "depart", day 10 (next week's Saturday, from the Days list), time "09:00". Must not be 3, and clean() must not turn it into 0."},{"name":"no place keeps the time","input":"{"text":"明天早上八點","now":"2026-11-11 10:00","places":["家","學校"]}","expect":"to "" with no invented place. After clean(), day 1 and time "08:00" are kept with by "depart", so the phone asks only where, offering 家 and 學校 as taps."},{"name":"weekday not given by caller","input":"{"text":"週一早上七點半前到公司","now":"2026-11-14 22:30","places":["家","公司"]}","expect":"Code labels 2026-11-14 週六. to "公司", by "arrive", day 2, time "07:30". The model does no weekday arithmetic of its own."},{"name":"midnight tonight from a named start","input":"{"text":"半夜十二點從西門町回家","now":"2026-11-11 22:00","places":["家","學校"]}","expect":"from "西門町", to "家", by "depart", day 1, time "00:00". Must not be 12:00 or day 0."}]}

{"verdict":"For famous, unambiguous places like 合歡山, 日月潭 and 竹北高中 it returns a sensible name, county and plausible coordinates, and it correctly refuses nonsense like 阿巴阿巴. It breaks down on Taiwan's many duplicate names (中山公園, 中正國小, 火車站), which dead-end with no tap-to-choose options, on places abroad, where 'county' is undefined, and on wrong coordinates that cheap models give from memory, which nothing catches.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"Ambiguous places dead-end instead of asking back. Taiwan has dozens of 中山公園, 中正國小 and 文化中心, but the prompt can only return an empty answer, and the schema has no field for options to tap. The rules say to ask back with tappable options when guessing would be wrong.","evidence":"Prompt: "or it could be several places and the question gives no hint which, return name "" and lat 0, lon 0." Schema: obj({ name: S, county: S, lat: N, lon: N }) has no options field.","fix":"Add an options array to the schema: 2–4 short '名稱（縣市）' candidates when the place is ambiguous, empty otherwise. Have clean() pass the options through so the UI can show them as chips."},{"severity":"high","what":"The coordinates are recalled from model memory, which breaks 'never invent numbers' and 'code first'. A cheap model will give confident 4-decimal coordinates for a small school or village that can be kilometres off, and the user sees a forecast for the wrong spot with no sign anything is wrong. clean() only checks the global range, so a 'Taiwan' answer that lands in the sea or in China still passes.","evidence":"Example 2: {"name":"竹北高中","county":"新竹縣","lat":24.8389,"lon":121.0095}. That is 11 m precision from recall, and nothing verifies it. clean() checks only Math.abs(lat) > 90 || Math.abs(lon) > 180.","fix":"Longer term, let the model only normalise the name and county, and have code resolve the coordinates through the geocoder the app already uses (Google). Now: tell the model to refuse rather than estimate when it doesn't know the spot. In clean(), reject any answer whose county is one of Taiwan's 22 but whose coordinates fall outside Taiwan's bounding box (including 金門, 馬祖 and 東沙)."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Places abroad are undefined. clean() says anywhere on the map is allowed, but the prompt asks for a Taiwanese 'county or city'. For 東京 or 京都 the model may leave county empty, invent something, or refuse because the place is not in Taiwan.","evidence":"Prompt: "the county or city it is in". clean() comment: "(Anywhere on the map; ... abroad Google's forecast answers too.)"","fix":"Say explicitly: outside Taiwan, county is '國家 城市' in Taiwanese usage, e.g. '日本 東京'."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Colloquial names and broad areas are not covered. 小琉球, 清境, 101, 墾丁 and 阿里山 each need a rule for what to name and where to put the point. Without one, the model may refuse or pick an arbitrary point, such as the township centre instead of the visited area.","evidence":"Prompt only covers "a mountain: its summit; a town, park, school or sight: its centre".","fix":"Add: map nicknames and abbreviations to the usual full name (小琉球 → 小琉球（琉球鄉）, 屏東縣). For a scenic area or region, use the spot visitors go to (阿里山 → 阿里山森林遊樂區). For a township or district, use its main town."},{"severity":"low","what":"The prompt does not say how to spell the county. Taiwan uses both 台 and 臺, so if code later matches county names against government weather data, unnormalised output will miss.","evidence":"Answers use 南投縣 and 新竹縣 here, but 台中市 vs 臺中市 is unspecified.","fix":"Have clean() compare counties after a 台→臺 normalisation, as in the edit below. Use the same normalisation wherever code matches county names."}],"edits":[{"old":"'A person in Taiwan asks about the weather at a place. Say where that place is: its usual name in Traditional Chinese (台灣用語), the county or city it is in, and its coordinates in decimal degrees (a mountain: its summit; a town, park, school or sight: its centre).',","new":"'A person in Taiwan asks about the weather at a place. Say where that place is: its usual full name in Traditional Chinese (台灣用語; turn nicknames and short forms into it, e.g. 小琉球 → 小琉球（琉球鄉）, 101 → 台北101), the county or city it is in (in Taiwan one of the 22, e.g. 南投縣, 台中市; abroad: country and city, e.g. 日本 東京), and its coordinates in decimal degrees (a mountain: its summit; a town, park, school or sight: its centre; a township or district: its main town; a scenic area or region: the spot visitors go to, e.g. 阿里山 → 阿里山森林遊樂區).',","why":"Defines county for places abroad and covers nicknames and broad areas, so cheap models don't refuse or pick arbitrary points."},{"old":"'Only a real place you know. If it is not one, or it could be several places and the question gives no hint which, return name "" and lat 0, lon 0. Never guess.',","new":"'Only a real place whose location you actually know; if you are not sure where it is, do not estimate coordinates. If it is not a real place, return name "", county "", lat 0, lon 0, options []. If it could be several places (e.g. 中山公園, 中正國小, 火車站) and neither the place nor the question says which, return name "", lat 0, lon 0 and in options the 2 to 4 likeliest, each written as 名稱（縣市）, e.g. 中山公園（基隆市）. Otherwise options is []. Never guess.',","why":"Turns ambiguity into tap-to-choose options, as the rules require, and tells the model to refuse rather than invent coordinates."},{"old":"schema: obj({ name: S, county: S, lat: N, lon: N }),","new":"schema: obj({ name: S, county: S, lat: N, lon: N, options: arr(S) }),","why":"Gives the model a field for the clarify options. This assumes an array helper `arr` alongside `obj`, `S` and `N`."},{"old":"if (!name || !Number.isFinite(lat) || !Number.isFinite(lon) || Math.abs(lat) > 90 || Math.abs(lon) > 180 || (lat === 0 && lon === 0)) return { name: '', county: '', lat: 0, lon: 0 };","new":"const options = (Array.isArray(raw?.options) ? raw.options : []).map(o => str(o, 30)).filter(Boolean).slice(0, 4);
      const county = str(raw?.county, 20);
      const TW = ['臺北市','新北市','桃園市','臺中市','臺南市','高雄市','基隆市','新竹市','嘉義市','新竹縣','苗栗縣','彰化縣','南投縣','雲林縣','嘉義縣','屏東縣','宜蘭縣','花蓮縣','臺東縣','澎湖縣','金門縣','連江縣'];
      const inTW = lat > 20.5 && lat < 26.5 && lon > 116.5 && lon < 122.5;
      if (!name || !Number.isFinite(lat) || !Number.isFinite(lon) || Math.abs(lat) > 90 || Math.abs(lon) > 180 || (lat === 0 && lon === 0) || (TW.includes(county.replace(/台/g, '臺')) && !inTW)) return { name: '', county: '', lat: 0, lon: 0, options: options.length > 1 ? options : [] };","why":"Passes the clarify options through to the UI. Also rejects coordinates that contradict a Taiwanese county, a cheap, code-side check against invented coordinates."},{"old":"return { name, county: str(raw?.county, 20), lat: Math.round(lat * 1e4) / 1e4, lon: Math.round(lon * 1e4) / 1e4 };","new":"return { name, county, lat: Math.round(lat * 1e4) / 1e4, lon: Math.round(lon * 1e4) / 1e4, options: [] };","why":"Reuses the cleaned county and keeps the output shape consistent with the new options field."}],"examples":[{"name":"Ambiguous park, no hint","input":"{"question":"明天中山公園會下雨嗎","place":"中山公園"}","expect":"Must return name "", lat 0, lon 0 and 2–4 options like 中山公園（基隆市）, 中山公園（台中市）. Must not pick one and give its coordinates."},{"name":"Ambiguous name, but the question says which","input":"{"question":"週末台中的中正國小會很熱嗎","place":"中正國小"}","expect":"Must resolve to a school in 台中市 with coordinates inside Taiwan and options []. If there are several 中正國小 in 台中, it must return options within 台中市 rather than guess."},{"name":"Place abroad","input":"{"question":"下週東京會冷嗎","place":"東京"}","expect":"name 東京, county 日本 東京 (or equivalent country + city), coordinates near 35.68, 139.69. Must not refuse because it is not in Taiwan, and must not leave county empty."},{"name":"Colloquial island name","input":"{"question":"這週末小琉球浪大嗎","place":"小琉球"}","expect":"Must resolve to 小琉球/琉球鄉 in 屏東縣 at about 22.34, 120.37. Must not refuse or confuse it with 琉球 (沖繩)."},{"name":"Broad scenic area","input":"{"question":"明天阿里山看得到日出嗎","place":"阿里山"}","expect":"Must give 阿里山森林遊樂區 in 嘉義縣, around 23.51, 120.80. Must not give the 阿里山鄉 township centre or the city of 嘉義."},{"name":"Generic landmark with city in question","input":"{"question":"明天早上台南火車站會下雨嗎","place":"火車站"}","expect":"Must resolve to 台南火車站 in 台南市 at about 23.00, 120.21. Without the city in the question, the same place must instead return options, not a guess."}]}

{"verdict":"The example answers are usable: the English line is neutral and 12 words, and the Chinese line uses Taiwan's 聯準會 and only a figure the headlines give. The prompt is still too thin for cheap models on the cases that matter most: numbers crossing languages (which the check then silently drops), allegations reported as fact, outlets that disagree, Simplified or English sources, and over-long titles that clean() cuts mid-word.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"The prompt never says how to carry numbers across languages. Every story can be translated, and clean() checks the title's numbers against the original-language headlines. A correct conversion (3,252億 → 325.2 billion, 兩次 → 2) fails the check and the story silently gets no headline. The other risk is that the model converts units or relative dates itself and invents a figure.","evidence":"Prompt: "every number must be one the headlines give". clean(): numbersFrom(title, JSON.stringify(s.heads)). Example s1 is lang "en" built from all-Chinese heads, and s2 is lang "zh" from English heads. "2027年" passed only because the digits were copied literally.","fix":"Tell the model to copy numbers exactly as a headline writes them. Number words stay words (兩次 / two, 三人 / three) and digits stay digits. No 萬/億 ↔ million/billion conversion and no "next year" → year. If a number would need converting, leave it out."},{"severity":"high","what":"Nothing stops a "neutral" headline from dropping who made a claim and turning an allegation into fact. Stripping "framing" makes this more likely, because cheap models read 檢方指控 or "X says" as framing.","evidence":"Prompt: "Only what the headlines all say; no outlet’s adjectives or framing". There is no rule about attribution, accusations or quotes.","fix":"Add: keep who said or alleged it (檢方起訴, 涉嫌, X says), and never state a claim or accusation as fact."},{"severity":"medium","what":"When outlets disagree (death tolls, amounts), "all say" gives the model no instruction. The check accepts any number found in any headline, so one outlet's figure can be shown as the consensus.","evidence":"clean() tests against JSON.stringify(s.heads), the whole set of headlines, not against what they share. The prompt gives no rule for conflicting numbers.","fix":"Add: if the headlines give different numbers, or one gives a number the others don't, leave the number out."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Traditional script and Taiwan terms are not enforced when the sources are Simplified Chinese or English. Nothing in clean() catches a Simplified, mainland-term or wrong-language title. Names like 特朗普 or 美聯儲 would reach the user.","evidence":"The prompt gives only "Traditional Chinese (台灣用語)". clean() checks only length and numbers. s2's correct 聯準會 came from the model's own choice, not from the prompt.","fix":"Spell it out in the prompt: never Simplified even if the headlines are; use Taiwan's names (聯準會, 川普). Add a cheap script check in clean(): a zh title must contain CJK and an en title must not."},{"severity":"medium","what":"The length limits don't match. The prompt asks for ≤22字, but clean() allows 40 characters and passes the text through str(). An over-long title is either cut mid-phrase or shown far over the card's width. Cheap models count Chinese characters poorly.","evidence":"Prompt "≤ 22 字" and "≤ 14 words" vs clean() str(it.title, s.lang === 'zh' ? 40 : 120).","fix":"Reject over-long titles instead of truncating them, with modest slack (zh 30, en 110 characters). In the prompt, say the 22-character count includes digits and letters."},{"severity":"low","what":"Chinese titles use a half-width space and no full-width punctuation. Nothing in the prompt asks for 全形標點.","evidence":"Answer: "聯準會維持利率不變 預示2027年降息兩次".","fix":"Ask for full-width punctuation (，：「」) in zh titles."},{"severity":"low","what":"English titles from Chinese headlines must romanize people's names. A cheap model may invent a spelling, which breaks the no-invented-names rule.","evidence":"The prompt has no guidance on names. s1 avoided the problem only because no person appeared.","fix":"Use a name only as a headline gives it or in its well-known official form; otherwise use the person's role (the premier, 行政院長)."}],"edits":[{"old":"For each news story below (its outlets’ headlines), write one short neutral headline in the language asked: lang "zh": Traditional Chinese (台灣用語), ≤ 22 字; lang "en": English, ≤ 14 words.","new":"For each news story below (its outlets’ headlines), write one short neutral headline in the language its "lang" asks, whatever language the headlines are in. "zh": Traditional Chinese as Taiwan writes it (台灣用語 and Taiwan’s names, e.g. 聯準會, 川普; never Simplified even if the headlines are), full-width punctuation (，：「」), at most 22 characters counting every digit and letter. "en": English, at most 14 words, no Chinese characters.","why":"Makes the target script, Taiwan terms, punctuation and length counting explicit for cheap models, including when the sources are Simplified Chinese or English."},{"old":"Only what the headlines all say; no outlet’s adjectives or framing; every number must be one the headlines give. Return one item per story with its id.","new":"Say only what all the headlines agree on; drop any outlet’s adjectives, framing, questions and exclamation marks. If a headline reports a claim or accusation, keep who made it (e.g. 檢方起訴, 涉嫌, X says); never state it as fact. Numbers: copy each number exactly as a headline writes it (number words stay words, e.g. 兩次 / two; digits stay digits); no unit or currency conversion (no 萬/億 ↔ million/billion) and no turning "next year" into a year. If the headlines give different numbers, or a number would need converting, leave it out. Names: use a person’s or body’s name only as a headline gives it or in its well-known official form in the target language; if unsure, use their role (e.g. the premier, 行政院長). Return one item per story with its id; skip none.","why":"Covers cross-language numbers that the numbersFrom check would otherwise drop, attribution of claims, conflicting figures, and invented romanizations."},{"old":"const title = str(it.title, s.lang === 'zh' ? 40 : 120);","new":"const t0 = String(it?.title || '').trim();
        if (t0.length > (s.lang === 'zh' ? 30 : 110)) continue;
        const title = str(t0, s.lang === 'zh' ? 30 : 110);","why":"Drops over-long titles instead of cutting them mid-phrase or letting them overflow the card; the limit sits close to the prompt's 22字 / 14 words."},{"old":"if (title && numbersFrom(title, JSON.stringify(s.heads))) out[s.id] = { [s.lang]: title };","new":"const hasCjk = /[\u4e00-\u9fff]/.test(title);
        if (title && hasCjk === (s.lang === 'zh') && numbersFrom(title, JSON.stringify(s.heads))) out[s.id] = { [s.lang]: title };","why":"A cheap script check: a zh title must contain Chinese characters and an en title must not, so wrong-language titles are never shown."}],"examples":[{"name":"zh→en with 億 amounts and percent","input":"{"stories":[{"id":"t1","lang":"en","heads":["台積電第三季淨利3,252億元 年增54%","台積電Q3獲利創新高 年增54%","AI需求強 台積電季獲利年增54%"]}]}","expect":"An English headline of ≤14 words that may keep "54%". It must not convert 3,252億 into any billion figure; leave the amount out. No "record" unless all headlines say it (one says 創新高, two don't), so omit it."},{"name":"en→zh with conflicting death tolls","input":"{"stories":[{"id":"q1","lang":"zh","heads":["Strong quake in Hualien kills at least 12","Hualien earthquake death toll rises to 15","Taiwan quake: rescuers search collapsed buildings"]}]}","expect":"A Traditional Chinese line, e.g. 花蓮強震釀死傷，搜救持續, with full-width punctuation and ≤22 characters. It must not show 12 or 15, because the outlets disagree and one gives no toll."},{"name":"Accusation must keep attribution","input":"{"stories":[{"id":"c1","lang":"zh","heads":["檢方起訴前議員涉貪 收賄500萬元","前議員遭控收賄500萬 檢起訴","涉收賄500萬 前市議員被起訴"]}]}","expect":"It must keep 檢方起訴 or 涉嫌, e.g. 前市議員涉收賄500萬元遭起訴. It must not say 前議員收賄500萬 as fact, and must not add the councillor's name or party."},{"name":"Simplified source to Taiwan Traditional","input":"{"stories":[{"id":"p1","lang":"zh","heads":["特朗普宣布对华加征关税","美国总统特朗普签署行政令 对中国商品加征关税"]}]}","expect":"Traditional script with Taiwan terms: 川普, 關稅, 中國 or 對中. No Simplified characters and no 特朗普. Add no tariff rate, since the headlines give none."},{"name":"Single sensational outlet","input":"{"stories":[{"id":"y1","lang":"en","heads":["Shocking! Typhoon Krathon slams Kaohsiung, city paralysed?!"]}]}","expect":"A plain English line such as "Typhoon Krathon hits Kaohsiung". No "Shocking", "paralysed", question or exclamation marks, and nothing the headline doesn't say."},{"name":"zh→en with a person's name and Chinese number words","input":"{"stories":[{"id":"n1","lang":"en","heads":["卓榮泰視察災區 三人仍失聯","行政院長卓榮泰赴災區 三人失聯"]},{"id":"n2","lang":"zh","heads":["Fed cuts rates by a quarter point","Federal Reserve lowers rates 25 basis points"]}]}","expect":"n1: "Premier Cho Jung-tai" or just "the premier", with no invented spelling; "three missing" written in words, not "3". n2: 聯準會 with no invented figure; 降息1碼 or 25個基點 must not be newly derived, so the plain 聯準會降息 is acceptable. Both items are returned with their ids."}]}
